{% set plan = states.sensor.hoymiles_hit_tariff_charge_plan %}
{% if plan is not none %}
{% set operator = states('input_select.hoymiles_tariff_operator') %}
{% set group = states('input_select.hoymiles_tariff_type') %}
{% if plan.attributes.tariff_profile_expired | default(false) %}
⚠️ **The tariff profile has expired. Automatic charging is blocked.**
Update the integration or select **Manual** with current prices.

{% endif %}
{% if operator == 'Manual' %}
**Manual mode · {{ group }}**

Time periods and total marginal prices are taken from the manual fields below.
{% elif plan.attributes.tariff_profile_supported | default(false) %}
**{{ plan.attributes.tariff_operator_name }} · {{ group }}**<br>
{% if is_state('input_boolean.hoymiles_tariff_advanced_view', 'on') %}
Assumed supplier: **{{ plan.attributes.tariff_supplier_assumption }}**<br>
Price list: **{{ plan.attributes.tariff_profile_year }}** · season:
**{{ 'summer' if plan.attributes.tariff_profile_season == 'summer'
   else 'winter' }}**<br>
{% endif %}
Current period: **{{ plan.attributes.tariff_profile_current_zone }}** ·
**{{ plan.attributes.tariff_profile_current_price }} PLN/kWh**<br>
Low-cost hours: **{{ plan.attributes.tariff_profile_low_windows }}**<br>
{% if group == 'G13' %}
Medium period: **{{ plan.attributes.tariff_profile_medium_windows }}**<br>
{% endif %}
Weekend in low-cost period:
**{{ 'yes' if plan.attributes.tariff_profile_weekend_low else 'no' }}** ·
public holidays: **{{ 'yes' if plan.attributes.tariff_profile_holiday_low else 'no' }}**

{% if is_state('input_boolean.hoymiles_tariff_advanced_view', 'on') %}
| Period | Indicative price |
|---|---:|
| G11 (comparison) | {{ plan.attributes.tariff_profile_g11_price }} PLN/kWh |
| Low-cost | {{ plan.attributes.tariff_profile_low_price }} PLN/kWh |
{% if group == 'G13' %}| Medium | {{ plan.attributes.tariff_profile_medium_price }} PLN/kWh |
{% endif %}| Peak | {{ plan.attributes.tariff_profile_peak_price }} PLN/kWh |

[Official DSO tariffs]({{ plan.attributes.tariff_profile_source_url }})
{% endif %}
{% else %}
⚠️ Profile **{{ operator }} · {{ group }}** is not supported.
Automatic charging will remain blocked. Select another group
or the **Manual** profile.
{% endif %}

{% if is_state('input_boolean.hoymiles_tariff_advanced_view', 'on') %}
Prices include energy from the regional incumbent supplier and variable
gross distribution charges. Fixed fees are excluded. With another
supplier, select **Manual** and enter prices from your own bill.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% set plan = states.sensor.hoymiles_hit_tariff_charge_plan %}
{% if plan is not none %}
{% set status = plan.attributes.status_code | default('missing_data', true) %}
{% set slots = plan.attributes.planned_slots | default([], true) %}
{% set low_direct = plan.attributes.remaining_low_direct_import_kwh
   | default(0) | float(0) %}
{% set expensive = plan.attributes.remaining_expensive_import_kwh
   | default(0) | float(0) %}
{% set physical = plan.attributes.capacity_or_power_shortfall_kwh
   | default(expensive) | float(0) %}
{% set terminal = plan.attributes.terminal_shortfall_kwh
   | default(0) | float(0) %}
{% if status in ['missing_data', 'optimizer_error', 'unsupported_profile',
                 'expired_profile', 'soc_limits_conflict'] %}
⚠️ **The automation requires attention.**
{{ states('sensor.hoymiles_hit_tariff_charge_plan') }}
{% elif status == 'hard_reserve_unavailable' %}
⚠️ **The base Self-Use reserve cannot be restored.** The hardware or
an active charging limit prevents the required Grid Charge operation.
The automation will remain in a safe mode. Details are available in
advanced data.
{% elif status == 'no_cheap_window' %}
⚠️ **There is no low-cost period before the forecast shortage.**
The automation will not start Grid Charge in a high-cost period.
{% elif status == 'not_economically_beneficial' %}
ℹ️ **Charging intentionally skipped.** A low-cost period is available, but
the price spread does not cover conversion losses, battery wear, and
the required savings margin. The automation remains in Self-Use
instead of running an uneconomical cycle.
{% elif expensive > 0.01 or terminal > 0.01 %}
⚠️ **The plan is only partially feasible.** The automation will use the available
low-cost periods but cannot cover all forecast demand.
{% if expensive > 0.01 %}After accounting for battery power and capacity,
there will remain **{{ expensive | round(2) }} kWh** of import in a higher-cost period.{% endif %}
{% if terminal > 0.01 %}The required reserve at the end of the horizon
will be short by **{{ terminal | round(2) }} kWh**.{% endif %}
{% elif status == 'shortage_in_low_period' %}
✅ **The plan is correct.** The remaining energy demand occurs only in the low-cost
period, so the home will import it directly without battery conversion losses.
{% elif status == 'no_charge_needed' %}
✅ **The battery does not need charging.** Forecast PV and stored battery energy
will last until the next low-cost period while preserving the reserve.
{% elif status == 'no_discount_window' %}
ℹ️ **The G11 tariff has no lower-cost period.** The automation remains in Self-Use
because shifting energy through the battery would not reduce cost.
{% elif slots %}
✅ **Plan ready.** The automation will import only the calculated energy
in selected low-cost slots and preserve the required battery reserve.
{% else %}
✅ **Grid Charge is not needed.** The current balance does not require
additional battery charging.
{% endif %}

{% if low_direct > 0.01 %}
ℹ️ **{{ low_direct | round(2) }} kWh** is the forecast direct import
in the low-cost period. The automation selects it intentionally to avoid
battery conversion losses.
{% endif %}

The automation bases its decision on **conservative values used by the model**,
not on the raw forecast displayed by Solcast.

**PV remaining today:**
{{ plan.attributes.model_input_forecast_remaining_today_kwh
   | default(plan.attributes.forecast_remaining_today_kwh
   | default('—', true)) }} kWh<br>
**PV tomorrow:**
{{ plan.attributes.model_input_forecast_tomorrow_kwh
   | default(plan.attributes.forecast_tomorrow_kwh
   | default('—', true)) }} kWh<br>
**Conservative daily home consumption:**
{{ plan.attributes.model_input_average_daily_load_kwh
   | default(plan.attributes.robust_average_daily_load_kwh
   | default(plan.attributes.average_daily_load_kwh
   | default('—', true))) }} kWh<br>
**Average night consumption:**
{{ plan.attributes.model_input_average_night_load_kwh
   | default(plan.attributes.average_night_load_kwh
   | default('—', true)) }} kWh<br>
**Battery reserve:** {{ plan.attributes.reserve_soc_percent
   | default(0) }}% SOC<br>
**Forecast SOC at the end of the plan:**
{{ plan.attributes.ending_battery_soc_percent | default(0) }}%

{% if plan.attributes.planning_horizon_limited | default(false) %}
⚠️ The horizon is temporarily limited because the day-three forecast
is unavailable or stale. The plan retains an additional safety margin.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

# ⚡ Your installation is working for you
{% set revenue = states('sensor.hoymiles_rce_revenue_daily')
   | float(0) %}
{% set energy = states(
   'sensor.hoymiles_rce_grid_export_energy_daily') | float(0) %}
{% set average = revenue / energy if energy > 0 else 0 %}
**Today the grid received {{ energy | round(2) }} kWh**, and the calculated revenue at RCE prices is **{{ revenue | round(2) }} PLN**. The average achieved price is **{{ average | round(3) }} PLN/kWh**.
Every exported kilowatt-hour is settled at the price applicable at the time of export. Period meters retain data after Home Assistant restarts.

{% set periods = [
  ('Today', 'daily'),
  ('Week', 'weekly'),
  ('Month', 'monthly'),
  ('Year', 'yearly')
] %}
{% for label, period in periods %}
{% set revenue = states(
  'sensor.hoymiles_rce_revenue_' ~ period) | float(0) %}
{% set energy = states(
  'sensor.hoymiles_rce_grid_export_energy_' ~ period) | float(0) %}
{% set average = revenue / energy if energy > 0 else 0 %}
- **{{ label }}:** **{{ average | round(3) }} PLN/kWh** ·
  {{ revenue | round(2) }} PLN · {{ energy | round(2) }} kWh
{% endfor %}
